cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "VTQ — Velri Trellis Quant: Hardware-Co-Designed 16x256 Trellis Weight Quantization for LLMs"
message: "If you use VTQ, its benchmarks, or its quantization kernels in research or software, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "Vemloir"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/velri-inference/vtq-research"
url: "https://velri-inference.github.io"
abstract: >-
  VTQ (Velri Trellis Quant, .vtq v2) is a hardware-co-designed Ungerboeck trellis
  weight quantization format built around self-contained 16x256 (4,096-weight)
  supertiles spanning 1.5-6.0 bits per weight (bpw). Shared identically across disk,
  AVX2 CPUs (vpshufb without AVX-512), and GPUs (FP32 / DP4A INT8, up to 1,476.9 GB/s
  or 96.4% peak HBM on NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell), VTQ achieves strictly lower
  teacher-forced KL divergence than EXL3 (mul1) and GGUF (imatrix) across 36/36
  neutral-calibration benchmark cells on Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, gemma-4-26B-A4B-it,
  and Qwen3.6-35B-A3B while quantizing 1.3-5.1x faster than EXL3.
keywords:
  - llm-quantization
  - weight-quantization
  - trellis-quantization
  - tcq
  - viterbi
  - exl3
  - gguf
  - moe
  - avx2
  - cuda
  - blackwell
  - velri
  - vtq
